
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
DA = DB [00]
DB = DC [01]
E,B,A are collinear [02]
DE ⟂ AB [03]
BF ⟂ BD [04]
CF ⟂ CD [05]
D,G,E are collinear [06]
G,C,A are collinear [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. B,A,E are collinear [02] & D,G,E are collinear [06] & AB ⟂ DE [03] ⇒  EB ⟂ DG [08]
002. EB ⟂ DG [08] & BF ⟂ BD [04] ⇒  ∠EBF = ∠GDB [09]
003. DA = DB [00] & DB = DC [01] ⇒  D is the circumcenter of \Delta CAB [10]
004. D is the circumcenter of \Delta CAB [10] & BF ⟂ BD [04] ⇒  ∠ABF = ∠ACB [11]
005. G,C,A are collinear [07] & D,G,E are collinear [06] & ∠EBF = ∠GDB [09] & E,B,A are collinear [02] & ∠ABF = ∠ACB [11] ⇒  ∠GCB = ∠GDB [12]
006. ∠GCB = ∠GDB [12] ⇒  D,G,B,C are concyclic [13]
007. BF ⟂ BD [04] & CF ⟂ CD [05] ⇒  ∠FCD = ∠FBD [14]
008. BF ⟂ BD [04] & CF ⟂ CD [05] ⇒  ∠FBD = ∠DCF [15]
009. ∠FCD = ∠FBD [14] ⇒  D,B,C,F are concyclic [16]
010. D,G,B,C are concyclic [13] & D,B,C,F are concyclic [16] ⇒  D,G,B,F are concyclic [17]
011. D,G,B,C are concyclic [13] & D,G,B,F are concyclic [17] ⇒  F,C,D,G are concyclic [18]
012. F,C,D,G are concyclic [18] ⇒  ∠FCD = ∠FGD [19]
013. B,F,D,G are concyclic [17] ⇒  ∠BFG = ∠BDG [20]
014. D,G,E are collinear [06] & ∠FCD = ∠FGD [19] & ∠FBD = ∠DCF [15] & ∠BFG = ∠BDG [20] ⇒  GF ⟂ DG [21]
015. GF ⟂ DG [21] & EB ⟂ DG [08] ⇒  GF ∥ EB [22]
016. GF ∥ EB [22] & E,B,A are collinear [02] ⇒  FG ∥ AB
